{"file":"mergify-v1.zip","bytes":697287,"status":"已读取","plugins":[{"path":".claude-plugin/plugin.json","name":"mergify","description":"Skills for the Mergify CLI: manage merge queues, stacked pull requests, Test Insights (flaky tests, quarantine), merge protections, and Mergify configuration directly from the terminal.","license":"Apache-2.0","repository":"https://github.com/Mergifyio/mergify-cli","homepage":"https://mergify.com","keywords":["git","pr","stacked-prs","merge-queue","ci","test-insights","flaky-tests","quarantine","freeze","config","push","commit","branch","rebase","checkout","workflow"]},{"path":".codex-plugin/plugin.json","name":"mergify","description":"Skills for the Mergify CLI: merge queue, stacked pull requests, CI Insights, merge protections, and configuration.","version":"1.0.0","license":"Apache-2.0","repository":"https://github.com/Mergifyio/mergify-cli","homepage":"https://mergify.com","keywords":["git","pr","stacked-prs","merge-queue","ci","test-insights","flaky-tests","quarantine","freeze","config","push","commit","branch","rebase","checkout","workflow"]}],"skills":[{"path":".claude/skills/releasing/SKILL.md","name":"releasing","description":"Cut and ship a new release of the `mergify` CLI — build the draft release with its platform binaries, publish it, and verify PyPI and the Homebrew tap picked it up. Use when asked to release, cut a release, ship a new version, publish a release, tag a version, or when a release run failed and needs recovery. Triggers on \"release\", \"new version\", \"cut a release\", \"ship it\", \"publish the release\", \"bump the version\", \"release failed\", \"PyPI publish failed\".","headings":["Releasing `mergify-cli`","Guardrails","Stage 1 — build the draft","or, only when a specific version is needed:","Stage 2 — publish","Verify after publishing","Recovery"],"name_hint":"releasing"},{"path":"skills/mergify-ci/SKILL.md","name":"mergify-ci","description":"Use Mergify CI commands to upload JUnit test results, detect git references, manage CI scopes, and retrieve merge queue metadata. ALWAYS use this skill when working with CI pipelines, test result uploads, quarantine, scopes detection, or merge queue CI context. Triggers on CI, JUnit, test results, quarantine, scopes, git refs, CI insights.","headings":["Mergify CI Commands","Overview","Commands","Authentication","JUnit Processing (`junit-process`)","Git References (`git-refs`)","Output:","Base: abc1234","Head: def5678","Consume values in a shell script without parsing:","Or with jq:","Scopes (`scopes`)","Detect scopes from changed files","Detect scopes with explicit base/head","Write detected scopes to a file","Scopes Send (`scopes-send`)","Send specific scopes","Send scopes from a JSON file (produced by `mergify ci scopes --write`)"],"name_hint":"mergify · ci"},{"path":"skills/mergify-config/SKILL.md","name":"mergify-config","description":"Use Mergify config commands to validate configuration files, simulate Mergify actions, and write Mergify configuration. ALWAYS use this skill when validating, writing, editing, or simulating Mergify config. Triggers on config validate, config simulate, mergify configuration, mergify.yml, .mergify.yml, merge queue config, workflow rules, conditions.","headings":["Mergify Configuration Management","Overview","Commands","Configuration File Detection","Validating Configuration (`validate`)","Validate auto-detected config file","Validate a specific file","Simulating Actions (`simulate`)","Writing and Editing Configuration","Documentation index","Key reference pages","Workflow","Common Patterns","Test config changes before pushing","Edit your .mergify.yml locally, then:","If both look good, commit and push","CI validation gate"],"name_hint":"mergify · config"},{"path":"skills/mergify-events/SKILL.md","name":"mergify-events","description":"Use `mergify events` to browse the Mergify activity log — every event Mergify recorded for a repository or one pull request (queue enters/leaves, merges, commands, CI Insights, freezes), as a human timeline or JSON. ALWAYS use this skill when investigating what Mergify did to a PR or repository and when, reconstructing a pull request's merge-queue lifecycle, auditing Mergify actions, or filtering events by type. Triggers on activity log, event log, events, what did Mergify do, queue lifecycle, queue history, event timeline, event_type, action.queue.","headings":["Mergify Events","Overview","The window rule (the one thing to get right)","Reading the timeline","JSON contract","When to use something else"],"name_hint":"mergify · events"},{"path":"skills/mergify-merge-protections/SKILL.md","name":"mergify-merge-protections","description":"Use Mergify merge protections to control when PRs merge — PR dependencies (Depends-On header), delayed merges (Merge-After header), and scheduled freezes (CLI). ALWAYS use this skill when managing merge freezes, deployment windows, temporarily blocking merges, setting up PR dependencies, blocking a PR on another PR, coordinating cross-repo merges, scheduling a merge for a specific time, or adding Depends-On or Merge-After headers to PRs. Triggers on freeze, scheduled freeze, merge freeze, deployment freeze, halt merges, depends on, dependency, block merge, merge after, merge later, schedule merge, delayed merge, cross-repo, merge protection.","headings":["Mergify Merge Protections","Depends-On","Syntax","Rules","With `mergify stack push`","When to suggest","Merge-After","Syntax","Supported timestamp formats (ISO 8601)","When to suggest","Combining Depends-On and Merge-After","Scheduled Freezes","Commands","Authentication","Creating a Freeze","Emergency freeze (starts now, no end time)","Scheduled maintenance window","Freeze with conditions (only freeze merges to main)"],"name_hint":"mergify · 合并 · protections"},{"path":"skills/mergify-merge-queue/SKILL.md","name":"mergify-merge-queue","description":"Use Mergify merge queue to queue/dequeue PRs, to monitor and inspect the queue, and to diagnose a dequeued PR — whether it is queued, why it was dequeued, where its CI failure is, and what to do next. ALWAYS use this skill when queuing or dequeuing a PR, checking queue status, investigating PR merge state, finding out why a PR left the queue, pausing/unpausing the queue, or debugging merge failures. Triggers on queue a PR, requeue, dequeue, dequeued, why was my PR dequeued, dequeue reason, merge queue, queue status, queue pause, queue show, pause, unpause, frozen, bisecting, batch, CI checks, CHECKS_FAILED, PULL_REQUEST_UPDATED.","headings":["Mergify Merge Queue","Overview","Queuing and Dequeuing a PR","Commands","Is the PR queued, dequeued, or never queued?","Diagnosing a dequeued PR","1. `mergify queue show <PR>` (start here)","2. The Mergify activity log (what surface 1 reads underneath)","3. The `Mergify Merge Queue` check run","4. The `# Merge Queue Status` comment","Dequeue reasons and what to do next","Checking Queue Status","Inspecting a PR in the queue","Queue States","Pausing and Unpausing","Troubleshooting"],"name_hint":"mergify · 合并 · queue"},{"path":"skills/mergify-stack/SKILL.md","name":"mergify-stack","description":"Use Mergify stacks for git push, commit, branch, and PR creation. ALWAYS use this skill when pushing code, creating commits, creating branches, or creating PRs. Triggers on push, commit, branch, PR, pull request, stack, stacked, git, rebase, checkout, reorder, move, sync, amend, note, revision history.","headings":["Mergify Stack Workflow","Stack Philosophy","Core Conventions","Common Mistakes","Commands","GitHub-native stacks (experimental, opt-in)","Amend Notes","Edit HEAD, then:","Or for a mid-stack commit (after the rebase that amended it):","CRITICAL: Check Branch Before ANY Commit","CRITICAL: Stash Local Changes Before Worktree-Modifying Operations","Starting New Work","Adding to Existing Stack","Conflict Resolution"],"name_hint":"mergify · stack"}],"commands":[],"readmes":[{"path":"README.md","headings":["Mergify CLI",